      <div type="clause" n="93.6">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Hn">Hn</ref> 93.6</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="Hn 93.6" corresp="#wit-lat"><pb n="609" ed="#liebermann"/>Dentes alii precisores<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="29" target="#Hn_93-6.lnote.oe.29"/>, alii canini<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="30" target="#Hn_93-6.lnote.oe.30"/>, alii molares<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="31" target="#Hn_93-6.lnote.oe.31"/>. Precisores dicuntur primi dentes hominis, quia omne quod accipit ipsi prius incidunt; sequentes canini dicuntur, quorum duo in dextera maxilla, duo sunt in sinistra, et dicti sunt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="32" target="#Hn_93-6.lnote.oe.32"/> canini, quia ad similitudinem caninorum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="33" target="#Hn_93-6.lnote.oe.33"/> dentium existunt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="34" target="#Hn_93-6.lnote.oe.34"/>, et canis ex ipsis ossa frangit sicut homo; et quod priores precidere<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="35" target="#Hn_93-6.lnote.oe.35"/> non possunt, illis tradunt, ut confringant; ultimi sunt molares, qui concisa<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="36" target="#Hn_93-6.lnote.oe.36"/> a prioribus uel confracta a<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="37" target="#Hn_93-6.lnote.oe.37"/> sequentibus molunt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="38" target="#Hn_93-6.lnote.oe.38"/> et inmassant<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="39" target="#Hn_93-6.lnote.oe.39"/>.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">New row (October 2026): Liebermann’s text transcribed from Gesetze I p. 609 (two independent readings of the page images, differences settled against the page)</note>
